  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The energy is given as, $E=-\\frac{R_{\\mathrm{H}}}{9}...(i)$\nWe know that,\n$\\begin{aligned}\nE_n & =-\\frac{R_{\\mathrm{H}}}{n^2} ...(ii)\\\\\nn^2 & =9 \\\\\nn & =3\n\\end{aligned}$\nWhen $n=3, l=0,1,2$\n$(3 s, 3 p, 3 d \\text { sub-shells) }$\nOrbitals present (i.e., degeneracy),\n$3 s=1,3 p=3,3 d=5$\nTotal number of orbital present $=3+1+5=9$",
    "image": null
  },
